# SecForge app-repo template — secret-hostile .gitignore
#
# Source of truth: ADR-0013 § Multi-layer prevention guardrails (layer 1).
# Patterns mirror infrastructure/openbao/policies/app-template.hcl scope:
# anything that could carry an outbound credential to disk gets blocked
# at git-stage time so it never reaches the repo.
#
# To update, bump templates/app-repo/.template-version in the platform repo
# and re-cp into each app per docs/03-runbooks/new-app-bootstrap.md.

# === SECRETS / CREDENTIALS — NEVER COMMIT ===
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.crt
*.cer

id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*

# Cloud-provider credentials shaped files (defense-in-depth — these should
# never have existed in this repo, but the pattern catches accidents).
**/credentials.json
**/service-account*.json
.aws/
.gcloud/

# === BUILD / TEST ARTIFACTS ===
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt
dist/
build/
node_modules/

# === EDITOR / OS ===
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# === LOGS ===
*.log
